    "body": "Affects `GlobalOkHttpClient.buildSSLFactory` in `framework/src/androidMain/kotlin/com/zhangke/framework/architect/http/GlobalOkHttpClient.kt`.\n\nThe HTTP client currently creates its SSL context with `SSL` and overrides its default protocols with `SSLv3`. This violates the `SSLContextSpec` usage rule, which accepts `TLSV1.2`, `TLSV1.3`, and `TLS`.\n\nI changed the context to use `TLS` and removed the `SSLv3` override. The existing trust-manager setup and returned socket factory remain unchanged, keeping the change limited to the protocol selection.\n\nOkHttp 4.12.0 already negotiates only TLS 1.2 and 1.3 by default, so no protocol filter was added.\n\nI found this while running the app under RVSec, a runtime checker for how apps use the Java crypto and TLS APIs.\n\nThe project builds with this change (`assembleDebug`).\n\nI'm a Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), working on a research project on Android app analysis. Happy to adjust this to the project's conventions.",
